// 01_meta.bund — Inspecting cluster mode from a Bund script.
//
// The `?cluster.meta` word reads the most-recent cluster-aware
// helper's per-thread cache.  When standalone, or when no `cls.*`
// word has run on the current thread, it returns nodata.  When a
// cluster read just ran, it returns:
//   { enabled, peers_queried, peers_answered, partial, failed[] }
// When a cluster write just ran, it returns:
//   { enabled, replication: { peers_attempted, peers_succeeded, hints_queued } }
//
// `cls.timeline` is a no-input read that returns {min_ts, max_ts}
// across the cluster, so it's the cheapest way to populate the meta.

cls.timeline             // pushes {min_ts, max_ts} on the stack
?cluster.meta.           // pushes meta to the workbench (eval returns workbench top)
